    {
      "id": "470be1c0-c274-4cf3-b04b-b259d5c0121a",
      "name": "Read me",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -660,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "## Cakemail suppressed + bounced\n\nAuth is the generic **Bearer Auth** credential per person:\n- `Cakemail [Cole]` -> account **1679383**\n- `Cakemail [Josh]` -> account **1761047**\n\nNo Postgres, no token in the file.\n\n**Before the first run:** pick the spreadsheet on the two Sheets nodes. Tabs must be named `Suppressed` and `Bounced`, each with a header row matching the column names.\n\n`account_id` is set explicitly on each fetch node. It CANNOT be read from the token: Josh PAT is parent-scoped, so `GET /accounts/self` returns the PARENT account 1594688 (\"Playbook Mail\"), not the sending sub-account. Verified live 2026-10-07. Same ids as lib/cakemail.js."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d675d89d-bb26-4e95-b426-9c683997d3ac",
      "name": "How bounces are fetched",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -660,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## How bounces are fetched\n\nCakemail has no account-wide bounce list, so bounces come from campaign logs.\n\nCampaigns scheduled in the last 30 days are expanded into one request per bounce type (`bounce_hb`, `bounce_sb`, `bounce_mb`, `bounce_df`, `bounce_fm`, `bounce_tr`, `bounce_cr`, `bounce_ac`, `bounce_ar`) because the API `filter` only accepts a single `type==` value.\n\nThat is 9 requests per campaign per person. To widen the window, change the Filter node AND the `start_time` query param together.\n\nThe two people's branches are independent on purpose — no Merge, so one person having no campaigns in the window cannot stall the other."
      }
    },
